    {
      "heading": "Trivia",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "• Historically, it is yet to be confirmed whether Vikings wore padded armor. Assuming that they did, padded armor plausibly provided comfort as much as protection, more so if worn underneath mail armor (though it provided decent protection, mail armor did little to absorb or dissipate the force of a blow, resulting in bruises at best and broken bones at worst)."
    }
